  "query_preview": "/Thursday through Monday/...\nIssued 359 AM MDT MON JUL 6 2026\nOn Thursday, an upper trough moving by to our north will cool \ntemperatures to near normal. Breezy conditions with gusts 20-35 \nmph will continue across southern Idaho. An upper ridge will \nbuild over the southern Great Basin on Friday, then shift east \nto the Rocky Mountains and Northern Plains over the weekend into\nearly next week. Meanwhile, a trough will be nearly stationary \noff the Pacific Northwest coast. The ridge will bring hotter \ntemperatures starting Friday, although the trough should keep \nthe hottest temperatures east of our area. Highs in the lower \nvalleys are forecast to reach the upper 90s, but a slight shift \nof the ridge further west would push lower elevations over 100 \ndegrees. Conditions will remain dry with breezy winds under \nsouthwest flow aloft. By Monday, monsoon moisture may start to \nrotate around the ridge into our area. This would reintroduce \nshower and thunderstorm potential, likely continuing beyond \nMonday.",
